---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import GuideList from "../../components/GuideList.astro";
import Simple from "../../layouts/Simple.astro";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles", ({ data }) => data.section === "pricing")).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);
---
<Simple
  title="Analytics pricing"
  description="DataFast, PostHog, Amplitude, and Mixpanel pricing for founders, with the published steps from each vendor."
  kicker="Pricing"
  lede="Some analytics products publish a monthly tier. Others publish a free allowance and then charge for volume. These guides show the published steps."
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Pricing" }]}
>
  <p>DataFast, the analytics product at datafa.st, publishes monthly event tiers on its homepage. Starter starts at $9 and Growth at $19. The <a href="/pricing/datafast/">DataFast pricing</a> guide is that ladder, as of 25 November 2026. datafa.st/pricing returns 404, so the homepage is the source. The <a href="/reviews/datafast/">DataFast review</a> covers what the product is, and which other companies share the name.</p>
  <p>PostHog, Mixpanel, and Amplitude publish a free event allowance and then charge for volume. The useful question is what the first paid step costs at your volume. Plausible and Fathom price marketing analytics differently, and GA4’s standard product is free. Those figures are also compared on the <a href="/alternatives/">alternatives hub</a> and the <a href="/compare/">compare hub</a>.</p>
  <p>DataFast amounts are as of 25 November 2026. PostHog, Amplitude, and Mixpanel amounts are as of 24 November 2026 unless a page dates a figure later. Where a vendor only publishes “starts at $0” or a calculator, the guide says the price is an estimate or a quote.</p>
  <section slot="wide" class="band band-yellow">
    <div class="article-wide">
      <h2>Pricing guides</h2>
      <GuideList
        items={articles.map((article) => ({
          href: `/${article.id}/`,
          title: article.data.title,
          description: article.data.description,
        }))}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</Simple>
